ument_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 186, \"text\": \"Banksia lemanniana Banksia lemanniana, commonly known as the yellow lantern banksia or Lemann's banksia, is a species of woody shrub of the family Proteaceae native to Western Australia.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 187, \"end\": 328, \"text\": \"It generally grows as an open shrub or small tree to five metres (15 ft) high with stiff serrated leaves, and unusual hanging inflorescences.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 329, \"end\": 488, \"text\": \"Flowering occurs over summer, the greenish buds developing into oval flower spikes before turning grey and developing the characteristic large woody follicles.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 489, \"end\": 593, \"text\": \"It occurs within and just east of the Fitzgerald River National Park on the southern coast of the state.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 594, \"end\": 640, \"text\": \"\\\"Banksia lemanniana\\\" is killed by bushfire and\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 625, \"text\": \"Page information Concept URI Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Create a book Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikidata species of plant endemic to Western Australia Lemann 's banksia Yellow lantern banksia edit Language Label Description Also known as default for all languages No label defined – English Banksia lemanniana species of plant endemic to Western Australia Lemann 's banksia Yellow lantern banksia Statements instance of taxon 0 references image Banksia lemanniana latebud.JPG 1,425 × 1,109 ; 1.01 MB 0 referenc